  "justification": "With certified distinct prime entries, each positive divisor is a unique subset product. Splitting the subset into left and right halves and inverting the odd right product selects exactly D congruent to 2^a-1 modulo 2^(a+1). Since D divides 2^(2^a)-1 and 2^a divides m, D divides 2^m-1. For even m the three odd factors m-1, m+1 and m^2+1 are pairwise coprime: each pair has gcd dividing 2. Their product is m^4-1. Thus the two remaining power tests are equivalent to the requested divisibility on this list. For the small-modulus rejection, an odd prime ell in the bad product has order dividing ell-1 and not dividing 2^a. If p is prime and p exceeds ell-1, this order cannot divide 2^a*p. If p is composite the candidate is already ineligible."
